re no amount  of bond would have been sufficient i  think she should have gotten no bond she  should have been remanded straight to  prison she's clearly not a threat of  society so i don't think that's the  issue but i do think she's a flight risk  obviously she fled to costa rica she  changed her appearance so much so that  she got surgery i mean obviously dying  her hair she used her sister's identity  all of these things show that she will  go to great lengths to hide to run to  not face charges so if she did it once i  think she'd do it again and i think the  court would have been justified in  saying no no bond at all now the good  news is it's such a high amount i don't  think it will ever be met and i think  she will remain in jail until the case  is tried yeah neima i'm sure you've had  that situation we say your honor my  client's not a flight risk and the judge  is like she literally flew out of the  country the bond makes sense there in  some sense nemo i'm struggling to see  both sides of this potential trial here  is there a defense here or do you think  the defense attorneys are merely just  looking for the best plea either way  what can they argue in her favor  yeah there's really no defense here  right it's just a case about you know  getting the best possible deal avoiding  a life sentence getting some mitigation  she's obviously very young because  armstrong's in for a world of hurt here  not just state  prison state murder charges and which  will likely get her in state prison  there's a federal hold as well so this  one was rare cases where the feds may  come after obviously u.s marshals had to  track her down another country get her  extradited so this is not a defensible  case hopefully if you're the her lawyers  you can come up with some of some global  resolution to get her out of prison  hopefully in 20 25 years that's the best  it's going to get for her yeah there's a  reason why they call it pleading because  she might do a lot of pleading in this  case to try to get the best offer  possible if that's even open to her well  when we come back a jury's decision is  handed down in california in the case of  eric holder as he's tried for the murder  of rapper nifty hustle  [Music]  welcome back reality tv star jerry  harris of the netflix show cheer is  sentenced to 12 years in federal prison  for sex crimes involving children the  sentence was handed down on wednesday in  september of 2020 harris was arrested on  charges in the production of child  pornography and for soliciting sex and  sexually explicit images for minors in  february of this year he pled guilty to  charges of child pornography and  crossing state lines to engage in sex  with a child harris admitted to  exchanging sexual images with upwards of  15 children in three different states  harris admitted he knew the children  were under age at the time while  harris's team argues for a six-year  sentence prosecutors advocated for a  15-year sentence in the end a federal  judge handed down a 12-year sentence  with eight years of supervised release  the judge noted harris used his  celebrity status and wealth to  manipulate and exploit children and a  man on trial in the for killing  california rapper nipsey hussell faces a  sentence of life in prison after a jury  convicted eric holder junior of first  degree murder this week  thirty-three-year-old nipsey hassell was  shot and killed in march of 2019 in  front of the rapper's marathon clothing  store in los angeles his accused killer  finally faced a jury trial after three  years of delays prosecutors say holders  shot nipsey hussle after the two men got  into a dispute when the rapper accused  him of being a snitch a medical examiner  found the rapper was shot at least 10  times with the bullets piercing his  lungs and severing his spinal cord after  less than two days of deliberations on  wednesday a jury found holder jr guilty  of first degree murder attempted murder  and assault with a d