ing in la when nipsey  hussle was shot and you saw the reaction  in the community how do you think the  community will respond to this  conviction  brian you're right that reaction at the  time of the shooting was severe it was  substantial and at the time i was  actually teaching and we couldn't talk  about anything else that entire day  because these kids who were in their  early 20s really were affected by this  you have to remember that hustle rose  above his circumstances he started out  as a gang member actually the same gang  that eric holder jr was in but he became  a rapper he actually was grammy  nominated and he was an inspiration to  his community he bought property he  opened businesses he hired people he  gave others an opportunity the same type  of opportunity he actually didn't have  so he was well loved and i think this  verdict is going to help  absolutely well thank you both and thank  you for joining us here on lawn and  crime daily we'll see you next time as  we discuss justice in america  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

